omx-clap-host (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.10.0
  * abi: record the baseline of 0.10.0 with make abi-baseline
  * hosting.json: impl links that point at code reading a limit, and links
    --check in contract-dir-check.sh
  * hosted_stage_limits.h: say why no number carries a description and the
    file stays out of Doxygen
  * packaging: require omx-contract 2.15.0, and pin the CI contract job to
    its tag
  * omx-clap-host: the LV2 worker's ring and poll are the declared ones,
    16384 bytes (#145)
  * install: the rendered headers, the TypeScript module and the definitions,
    with no floor on the unreleased contract
  * clap_host_limits.h: the banner names the file it is rendered from
  * ts/omx-clap-core-hosting: the hosting items as a TypeScript module,
    rendered from data/hosting.json
  * hosted_stage_limits.h: the hosted stage's numbers as
    OMX_HOSTED_STAGE_<FIELD>, rendered from data/hosting.json
  * data/hosting.json: the render word that frames clap_host_limits.h, and
    the header held to it byte for byte
  * install data/ into omx-contract's contract directory, and hold the header
    to its render
  * data/hosting.json: HOSTED_STAGE_LIMITS and HOSTING_CODES, declared where
    they are implemented
  * omx-clap-host: one transport for every plugin: set_bpm, set_bpb,
    transport, -t (#88)
  * stage: the lane copy of omx_clap_run_io as omx_clap_io_lane, and
    omx_clap_host_run_io over it (#88)
  * doc: omx-clap-host hands every plugin a transport: set_bpm, set_bpb,
    transport, -t (#88)
  * BUILDING: make test-jack-notes-out (#89)
  * omx-clap-host: effect_<N>:midi_out carries a plugin's note output (#89)
  * core: a plugin's note output in a lock-free ring the audio role reads;
    ABI 7 (#89)
  * omx_clap_midi.h: the adapter's MIDI form of a CLAP note, as one installed
    header (#89)
  * doc: a plugin's note and MIDI output reaches effect_<N>:midi_out (#89)
  * stage: the note ids' sink passes every event on to the stage's sink
  * tests: jack_lv2_e2e expects atom-in-unfed from the value-atom fixture and
    keeps midi-in-fed-empty on a two-MIDI twin (#131)
  * stage: a zone asked for before activate lasts across the bind (#86)
  * core: a note port that prefers MIDI_MPE gets raw MIDI (#86)
  * core: note ids beside the stage, bound at activate; ABI 6 (#86)
  * stage: note ids, an MPE zone and NOTE_END on a CLAP note input (#86)
  * doc: note ids, MPE and note end on a CLAP note input (#86)
  * private-refs-check: self-test arms only the dated-filename and
    dated-citation patterns can catch
  * docs: the atom input rule, and a README refusal that still refuses (#131)
  * lv2: host an atom control input that takes no MIDI (#131)
  * Refuse AI-attribution lines in commit messages: commit-msg hook and a
    pull request check
  * doc: the MIDI dialect carries sysex up to 256 bytes, eight per cycle
    (#118)
  * docs: what a plugin does with its parameters by itself (#87)
  * omx-clap-host: param_set and param_gesture on the feedback socket (#87)
  * core: a plugin's own parameter events, modulation, host gestures, rescan,
    clear and text (#87)
  * docs: the state root and state:makePath through omx-clap-host (#111)
  * omx-clap-host: a state root, so state:makePath is offered (#111)
  * omx-clap-host: param_info answers from the parameter contract (#120)
  * core: read and check a plugin's parameter contract at open (#120)

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:25:37 +0000
